2. Three Distinct Viability Objects

Definition 2.1 (Physical viability). The physical viability kernel  \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{phys}}  is the set of physical histories from which the settlement can maintain life-support, energy, and critical-resource constraints  K_S  indefinitely:

\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{phys}} = \{ h \in \mathcal{H}_{\mathrm{phys}} : \exists u(\cdot) \text{ s.t. } L(t), E(t), R(t) \in K_S \ \forall t \}.

Definition 2.2 (Institutional viability). The institutional viability kernel  \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{inst}}  is the set of histories from which the decision architecture can maintain functionality, auditability, and contestability constraints  K_I  indefinitely:

\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{inst}} = \{ h \in \mathcal{H} : \exists u(\cdot) \text{ s.t. } I(t) \in K_I \ \forall t \}.

Definition 2.3 (Governance viability — multi-agent). The governance viability kernel  \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{MG}}  is the set of states from which a decentralized strategy profile exists such that all constraints are satisfied for all disturbances and all possible deviations by other agents:

\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{MG}}(A) = \left\{ h \in \mathcal{K}_H : \exists \sigma_A \ \forall d \in D \ \forall \sigma_{-i} : z(t) \in K \ \forall t \right\}

where  \sigma_A  is an admissible decentralized strategy profile under authority allocation  A , and  \sigma_{-i}  ranges over all admissible strategy profiles of agents other than  i . The single-controller existence kernel

\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{plan}} = \{ h \in \mathcal{K}_H : \exists u(\cdot) \text{ s.t. } h_t \in \mathcal{K}_H \ \forall t \}

is the planning kernel and serves as an upper bound on what governance can achieve.

Proposition 2.4 (Nesting).  \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{MG}} \subseteq \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{plan}} \subseteq \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{phys}} \cap \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{inst}} .

Proof. Every trajectory in  \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{MG}}  is generated by a strategy profile, hence corresponds to at least one admissible control history, so belongs to  \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{plan}} . Every trajectory in  \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{plan}}  satisfies  K_S  and  K_I , hence belongs to both  \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{phys}}  and  \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{inst}} . ∎

Research Hypothesis 2.5 (Institutional early warning). In multiplanetary governance systems subject to delayed authority,  \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{inst}}  can become empty before  \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{phys}}  becomes empty. Institutional collapse may precede physical collapse by a measurable lead time. The measurable proxy for institutional integrity  I(t)  is defined in §17.

