4. Local Tangency Condition for Delayed Viability

Definition 4.1 (Contingent cone). For a closed set  \mathcal{K}_H \subseteq \mathcal{H}  and  h \in \mathcal{K}_H , the contingent cone  T_{\mathcal{K}_H}(h)  is the set of  v \in \mathcal{H}  such that

\liminf_{\varepsilon \downarrow 0} \frac{d_{\mathcal{K}_H}(h + \varepsilon v)}{\varepsilon} = 0.

Definition 4.2 (Evaluation map at zero). Define  \operatorname{Ev}_0 : \mathcal{H} \to \mathbb{R}^{n_c+n_d}  by  \operatorname{Ev}_0(v) = v(0) .

Proposition 4.3 (Necessary local tangency condition — cited). Under the Marchaud and Lipschitz conditions on  F  and if  \mathcal{K}_H  is closed with non-empty interior in  \mathcal{H} , a necessary condition for local viability at  h \in \mathcal{K}_H  is

\exists u \in U \ \forall d \in D: \quad F(h, u, d) \cap \operatorname{Ev}_0(T_{\mathcal{K}_H}(h)) \neq \emptyset.

If  F  is nondeterministic with adversarial  d , the robust viability condition may require

\exists u \in U: \quad F(h, u, d) \subseteq \operatorname{Ev}_0(T_{\mathcal{K}_H}(h)) \quad \forall d \in D.

Attribution. This follows from the Necula–Popescu–Vrabie framework for delay evolution inclusions.

Definition 4.5 (Local viability domain). The local viability domain is

\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{loc}} = \{ h \in \mathcal{K}_H : \exists u \in U \ \forall d \in D, \ F(h,u,d) \cap \operatorname{Ev}_0(T_{\mathcal{K}_H}(h)) \neq \emptyset \}.

Research Objective 4.6. Establish conditions under which  \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{loc}}  coincides with  \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{MG}}  for the class of governance systems considered here. This is an open problem requiring proof of a full viability theorem for the hybrid delayed inclusion with institutional constraints.

