9. Power Concentration: Gramian-Based Constraint

Definition 9.1 (Controllability Gramian). For the linearized critical infrastructure system  \dot{x} = Ax + Bu , the controllability Gramian is

\mathcal{W} = \int_0^\infty e^{At} BB^T e^{A^T t} dt.

Definition 9.2 (Vulnerability matrix — cited). The vulnerability matrix at node  k  has entries

\mathrm{VM}_{ij}^k = \int_0^T \left( \frac{\partial F_{ij}}{\partial u_k} \right)^2 dt

where  F_{ij}  is the flow on edge  (i,j)  and  u_k  is the input at node  k .

Definition 9.3 (Power concentration constraint).

K_P: \quad \frac{\max_k \|\mathrm{VM}^k\|_{\mathrm{op}}}{\frac{1}{N}\sum_{j=1}^N \|\mathrm{VM}^j\|_{\mathrm{op}}} \leq \rho_{\text{crit}}

with the supplementary resilience condition

\lambda_{\min}(\mathcal{W}) \geq \lambda_{\text{crit}}.

Proposition 9.4 (Interpretation). The VM row-norm inequality limits the inequality of physical influence over the network. The Gramian eigenvalue condition ensures the network remains controllable despite concentration limits.

