10. Delay Monotonicity: A Conditional Conjecture

Conjecture 10.1 (Conditional governance delay monotonicity). For a class of multiplanetary governance systems in which communication delay acts exclusively through the information/authority channel and satisfies the following structural conditions:

1. Delay affects only the information/measurement channel, not actuation;
2. The instantaneous control set  U  is independent of  \tau ;
3. There is no delay-induced stabilization;
4. The hazard dynamics are independent of  \tau ;
5. Delay does not create new beneficial feedback channels;

then

\tau_1 \leq \tau_2 \implies \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{MG}}(\tau_2) \subseteq \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{MG}}(\tau_1).

Definition 10.3 (Critical governance delay). If Conjecture 10.1 holds, define the critical governance delay

\boxed{ \tau^\star = \sup \{ \tau : \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{MG}}(\tau) \neq \emptyset \}. }

Research Hypothesis 10.4 (Governance phase boundary). There exists a critical delay  \tau^\star  such that for  \tau > \tau^\star ,  \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{MG}}(\tau) = \emptyset  for a specified governance architecture.

