19. Validation Metrics

Metric 1 (AUC). The hybrid model must predict governance failure at least 5 percentage points better (AUC) than a physical-only model.

Metric 2 (VM correlation). The VM-based centrality metric must correlate with  K_P  violations at  r > 0.5 .

Metric 3 (Early warning lead time). The kernel-distance early warning must precede physical failure indicators in >70% of failure scenarios.

Metric 4 (Critical delay detection). The critical delay  \tau^\star  must be detected in M2 simulations.

Metric 5 (Governance infeasibility before physical failure — new). The fraction of simulated trajectories in which  \mathcal{U}_G(h_t) = \emptyset  while physical stocks are still comfortably inside  K_S . This directly tests whether governance infeasibility can be detected before physical failure.

