Appendix D: Padé Approximation and the Multiplicity-Induced-Dominancy Property

D.1 Padé Approximation of the Delay Operator

The delay operator  e^{-s\tau}  admits a Padé rational approximation:

e^{-s\tau} \approx \frac{P_{m,n}(s\tau)}{Q_{m,n}(s\tau)},

where  P_{m,n}  and  Q_{m,n}  are polynomials of degrees  m  and  n , respectively.

D.2 Connection to Kummer Hypergeometric Functions

The Padé approximation of the exponential function is closely related to Kummer hypergeometric functions. Specifically, the remainder term of the Padé approximation can be expressed in terms of the confluent hypergeometric function  {}_1F_1 .

Recently, a link between the degenerate hypergeometric function and the zeros distribution of the characteristic function associated with linear delay-differential equations has been established. This link allows the characterization of the multiplicity-induced-dominancy (MID) property.

D.3 Multiplicity-Induced-Dominancy

Definition D.1 (MID property). For a linear delay-differential equation

\dot{x}(t) = A x(t) + B x(t-\tau),

the characteristic function is

\Delta(s) = \det(sI - A - B e^{-s\tau}).

The MID property holds if a real root of  \Delta(s) = 0  of maximal multiplicity dominates the spectral abscissa, i.e., determines the exponential decay rate of solutions.

The MID property provides a spectral interpretation of the Padé approximation: the poles of the Padé approximant approximate the dominant roots of the characteristic function.

D.4 From Spectral Approximation to Viability Kernel Approximation

Remark D.2. Approximation of the delay operator in the frequency domain does not automatically imply Hausdorff approximation of the viability kernel. The viability kernel depends on the dynamics in a set-valued manner; small changes in the dynamics near bifurcations or loss of invariance can produce discontinuous changes in the kernel.

Conjecture 5.3 (Restated). Under conditions (1)–(3) of §5, there exists  C > 0  such that

d_H(\mathcal{V}^\tau_{\mathrm{MG}}, \mathcal{V}^{\text{Padé}}_{\mathrm{MG}}) \leq C \epsilon_{m,n}(\tau).

Research Objective D.3. Prove Conjecture 5.3 using the Aubin–Frankowska framework for set-valued continuity and graphical convergence. The key steps would be:

