Appendix K: Computational Implementation Specification

K.1 Viability Kernel Computation via kd-Trees

The Viabilitree framework represents viability sets and approximations with kd-trees. The computation of the viability kernel is formulated as an active learning problem, and convergence of the algorithm has been proved.

Algorithm K.1 (kd-tree viability kernel approximation).

1. Initialize  \mathcal{K}^0 = K , the constraint set.
2. For  n = 0, 1, 2, \ldots :
   a. For each cell  \mathcal{C} \in \mathcal{K}^n , test whether there exists  u \in U  such that the reachable set  R(\mathcal{C}, u) \subseteq \mathcal{K}^n .
   b. If no such  u  exists, remove  \mathcal{C}  from  \mathcal{K}^{n+1} .
   c. Otherwise, keep  \mathcal{C}  in  \mathcal{K}^{n+1} .
3. Terminate when  \mathcal{K}^{n+1} = \mathcal{K}^n .

The resulting  \mathcal{K}^\infty  is the viability kernel approximation. The error bound is controlled by the discretization step  h :

d_H(\mathcal{V}, \mathcal{K}^\infty) \leq C h.

K.2 Padé Reduction Workflow

1. Replace the delay operator  e^{-s\tau}  with its Padé approximant of order  (m,n) .
2. Derive the finite-dimensional state-space representation of the Padé-reduced system.
3. Apply Algorithm K.1 to the reduced system.
4. Bound the approximation error using Conjecture 5.3 (when proved).

K.3 Multi-Agent Guaranteed Kernel Computation

For the multi-agent case, the guaranteed viability kernel  \mathcal{V}_i^{\text{guar}}  is computed as the largest set  \mathcal{S} \subseteq K_i  such that for all  h \in \mathcal{S} , there exists  u_i  such that for all  u_{-i} , the next state remains in  \mathcal{S} .

Algorithm K.2 (Guaranteed kernel computation).

1. Initialize  \mathcal{S}^0 = K_i .
2. For  n = 0, 1, 2, \ldots :
   a. For each  h \in \mathcal{S}^n , test whether  \exists u_i \ \forall u_{-i}: F(h, u_i, u_{-i}) \subseteq \mathcal{S}^n .
   b. If not, remove  h  from  \mathcal{S}^{n+1} .
3. Terminate when  \mathcal{S}^{n+1} = \mathcal{S}^n .

The fixed point  \mathcal{S}^\infty = \mathcal{V}_i^{\text{guar}} .

