Appendix L: Validation Metrics — Formal Definitions

L.1 Metric 1: AUC Improvement

Definition L.1. Let  \mathrm{AUC}_{\mathrm{hybrid}}  be the area under the ROC curve for the hybrid model’s prediction of governance failure, and  \mathrm{AUC}_{\mathrm{phys}}  for the physical-only model. The improvement requirement is

\mathrm{AUC}_{\mathrm{hybrid}} - \mathrm{AUC}_{\mathrm{phys}} \geq 0.05.

L.2 Metric 2: VM Correlation

Definition L.2. Let  \rho_{\mathrm{VM}}  be the Spearman rank correlation between the VM-based centrality metric and the occurrence of  K_P  violations across simulation runs. The requirement is

\rho_{\mathrm{VM}} > 0.5.

L.3 Metric 3: Early Warning Lead Time

Definition L.3. Let  T_{\mathrm{EW}}  be the time at which the kernel-distance early warning signal exceeds a threshold, and  T_{\mathrm{PF}}  the time of physical failure. The lead time is  \Delta T = T_{\mathrm{PF}} - T_{\mathrm{EW}} . The requirement is

\mathbb{P}(\Delta T > 0) > 0.7.

L.4 Metric 4: Critical Delay Detection

Definition L.4. The critical delay  \tau^\star  is detected in simulation if there exists a  \tau_{\mathrm{sim}}  such that the simulated viability kernel  \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{MG}}(\tau_{\mathrm{sim}})  is empty while  \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{MG}}(\tau) \neq \emptyset  for  \tau < \tau_{\mathrm{sim}} .

L.5 Metric 5: Governance Infeasibility Before Physical Failure

Definition L.5. The fraction of simulated trajectories in which  \mathcal{U}_G(h_t) = \emptyset  while physical stocks are still comfortably inside  K_S  (margin  > \delta  for some  \delta > 0 ):

F_{\mathrm{GI}} = \frac{\#\{t : \mathcal{U}_G(h_t) = \emptyset \text{ and } d(x_c(t), \partial K_S) > \delta\}}{\#\{t\}}.

This directly tests whether governance infeasibility can be detected before physical failure.

